/// getApiDoc() text for the property canister (see backend/shared/ApiDoc.mo).
import Shared "../shared/ApiDoc";

module {
  public func text() : Text {
    "# HomeGentic property canister\n\n" #
    "Holds the homes a user has registered, who may act on each one, and the rooms and fixtures inside it. Most other canisters take a `propertyId` from here.\n\n" #
    "## Reading\n" #
    "- `getMyProperties()` (query): the caller's own properties. Start here to get `propertyId`s.\n" #
    "- `getMyManagedProperties()` (query): properties the caller manages for someone else, with their role.\n" #
    "- `getProperty(id)` (query): one property, if the caller owns or manages it.\n" #
    "- `getRoomsByProperty(propertyId)` / `getRoom(id)` (query): rooms and the fixtures in them (appliances, model numbers, install dates).\n" #
    "- `getOwnershipHistory(propertyId)` (query): past owner transfers.\n" #
    "- `getInsurancePolicy(propertyId)` (query): the home insurance policy details the household saved (carrier, policy number, renewal date as YYYY-MM-DD, Coverage A and hurricane deductible), or null. HomeGentic doesn't check them with the insurer.\n" #
    "- `getInsuranceClaims(propertyId)` (query): the household's records of insurance claims on the home, newest date of loss first, each with its dated log (`log`: date, note). These are the household's own notes; HomeGentic doesn't file or track anything with the insurer.\n" #
    "- `getInventory(propertyId)` (query): the household's list of what's in the home (name, category, quantity, value in cents, purchase date, serial number, notes, and the room it's in, if any), for an insurance claim. Only the household can read it.\n" #
    "- `getHouseGuide(propertyId)` (query): the house guide the household wrote for sitters and guests (Wi-Fi name and password, alarm notes, trash and recycling days, where the water, gas and electrical shutoffs are, contacts, notes, and ids of photos shown with it), or null. Passwords and alarm codes are stored exactly as the household typed them.\n" #
    "- `listHouseGuideLinks(propertyId)` (query): the home's guide links (token, name, created, expires, revoked), newest first; older expired or turned-off links are cleared as new ones are made. Only callers with write access to the home see them.\n" #
    "- `getSharedHouseGuide(token)` (query): what a guide link shows: the guide and the home's street address. Anyone holding the token can read it until it expires or is revoked; unknown, revoked and expired links all return `#NotFound`.\n" #
    "- `guideSharesPhoto(token, propertyId, photoId)` (query): for HomeGentic's photo canister; true when the link is live for that home and its guide shows that photo.\n" #
    "- `getArchitecturalReviews(propertyId)` (query): the household's log of architectural review requests to the HOA or condo association (project, details, submitted date, status, decision date, conditions, approval letter document id, job id), newest first.\n" #
    "- `getSpecialAssessments(propertyId)` (query): special assessments the association levied on the home (title, amount in cents, due date, paid date or empty, notes, document id), latest due date first.\n" #
    "- `getCondoAssociationRecord(propertyId)` (query): for a condo, what the owner entered about the association's milestone inspection and structural reserve study (dates as YYYY-MM-DD or empty, document ids, notes), or null. HomeGentic doesn't check it with the association and it says nothing about whether a building is safe.\n" #
    "- `getHomeWarrantyPlan(propertyId)` (query): the home warranty plan (service contract) the household entered: company, plan name, contract number, claim contact, service-call fee in cents, start and renewal dates (YYYY-MM-DD), what it covers and excludes in the owner's words, and the contract's document id; or null. HomeGentic doesn't sell or rate these plans and checks nothing with the company.\n" #
    "- `getHomeWarrantyClaims(propertyId)` (query): claims the household filed under the home warranty plan (date filed, issue, claim number, linked job id, service fee paid in cents, outcome, notes), latest filed first.\n" #
    "- `getMortgageLoan(propertyId)` (query): the mortgage numbers the owner entered (lender, amount borrowed in cents, rate in thousandths of a percent, term in months, first payment date, original and current home value, monthly PMI and escrow in cents, a statement balance with its date), or null. Only the owner and co-owners can read it. It feeds a calculator in the app; nothing is checked with the lender.\n" #
    "- `getFloodZone(propertyId)` (query): the flood zone FEMA's National Flood Hazard Layer showed for the home's address when HomeGentic last looked it up (zone, subtype, whether it's a special flood hazard area, base flood elevation, map panel and its effective date, the matched address and coordinates, when it was checked), or null. It is what FEMA's map shows, not a flood forecast or an insurance requirement.\n" #
    "- `getMoveInPlan(propertyId)` (query): the household's move-in plan, or null: when it started, the ids of finished steps, and the tasks the owner added (title, details, area of the home, urgency `#Safety` / `#Repair` / `#Monitor`). The steps themselves are suggestions the app writes from the home's own records; tasks the owner added from an inspection report are the owner's reading of it, not an inspection.\n" #
    "- `getPropertyTaxYears(propertyId)` (query): the property-tax years the owner entered, newest first: market, assessed and taxable values in cents, the exemption status (`#Unknown`, `#NotApplying`, `#Applied`, `#Granted`, `#Denied`), the petition deadline from the TRIM notice and notes. Only the owner and co-owners can read them. Nothing is checked with the county.\n" #
    "- `getPulseInsurance(owner)` / `getPulseHomeFinance(owner)` / `getPulsePropertyTax(owner)` (query): only for HomeGentic's notification relay, which emails renewal, PMI and property-tax deadline reminders. Any other caller gets `#NotAuthorized`.\n" #
    "- `getSuccessor(propertyId)` (query): the successor the owner named for the home record (name, email, relationship, the successor link's token, when it was named), or null. Owner only.\n" #
    "- `getSuccessionInvite(token)` (query): what a successor link shows: the home (identity and verification evidence blanked), the successor's name and the waiting period in days; null for an unknown link.\n" #
    "- `getOpenSuccessionClaim(propertyId)` (query): the open successor claim on the home, or null. Owner and co-owners only. `getMySuccessionClaims()` (query): the claims the caller opened, newest first.\n" #
    "- `listSuccessionClaimsForReview()` / `getSuccessionProof(claimId)` (query): HomeGentic administrators only.\n" #
    "- `getSuccessionNotice(claimId)` / `getNotificationEvents(afterSeq, limit)` (query): only for HomeGentic's notification relay, which emails the household about successor claims. Any other caller gets `#NotAuthorized`.\n" #
    "- `relayFloodTarget(propertyId, user)` (query) and `relaySetFloodZone(propertyId, user, result)`: only for HomeGentic's own server, which looks the address up with FEMA for a user who has a role on the home. Any other caller gets `#NotAuthorized`.\n\n" #
    "## Questions over the whole record (OQL)\n" #
    "- `schema()` (query): a JSON catalogue of the household's records about each home: `homes`, `rooms`, `fixtures`, `insurance_policies`, `insurance_claims`, `inventory_items`, `warranty_plans`, `warranty_claims`, `mortgages`, `tax_years`, `hoa_assessments`, `hoa_reviews`, `flood_zones` and `move_in_tasks`, with every field, its type and what it means. The house guide is not included.\n" #
    "- `execute(oql)` (query): runs one JSON query over one of those entities and returns rows of named cells, filtered, grouped and added up here, e.g. `{\"start\":\"inventory_items\",\"aggregate\":[{\"fn\":\"sum\",\"field\":\"valueCents\",\"as\":\"total\"}]}`. The keys are the same as on the job canister's `execute`. Without a `propertyId` condition (for `homes`, `id`) it covers the homes the caller owns; to read a home the caller co-owns, manages or views, add a `propertyId` `eq` or `in` condition (at most 20 homes). Each home is read under the same rule as its getter: any role for most records, owner and co-owners only for `mortgages` and `tax_years`. Homes the caller has no role on return nothing. Everything here is the household's own entry, not checked with insurers, lenders, the county or FEMA. Read-only and free; works in read-only sessions. A malformed query is rejected with a message starting \"OQL:\".\n\n" #
    "## Changing\n" #
    "- `registerProperty(args)`: adds a home. `state` is a 2-letter code, `zipCode` 5 digits or ZIP+4, `squareFeet` 1 to 100,000. Free accounts can register 1 property and Pro accounts 20. Registering an address you already own returns that home unchanged and creates nothing. If another user has verified that address, the call is refused with `#DuplicateAddress`. If another user has claimed it without verifying, `#AddressConflict` gives the end of a 7-day window for resolving it.\n" #
    "- `submitVerification(propertyId, method, documentHash, nameOnDoc)`: asks HomeGentic to verify ownership from a document the user uploaded in the web app. It moves the property to `#PendingReview`. A HomeGentic administrator approves it.\n" #
    "- `createRoom`, `updateRoom`, `deleteRoom`, `addFixture`, `updateFixture`, `removeFixture`: edit rooms and fixtures. `deleteRoom` and `removeFixture` can't be undone.\n" #
    "- `setInsurancePolicy(propertyId, policy)`: saves the home's insurance policy details, or clears them with null. Needs write access to the home (owner, co-owner or manager). `carrier` is required (up to 100 characters), `policyNumber` up to 60, `renewalDate` a real date written YYYY-MM-DD. `coverageACents` and a dollar hurricane deductible are in cents; a percent hurricane deductible is a whole percent of Coverage A, 1 to 25. This only records what the policy says: it doesn't contact the insurer or change the policy. The details are removed when the home is transferred to a new owner.\n" #
    "- `createInsuranceClaim(propertyId, input)` / `updateInsuranceClaim(claimId, input)`: start or edit a claim record: `title` (required, up to 100 characters), `dateOfLoss` (YYYY-MM-DD), `cause`, `description`, `claimNumber`, `adjusterName`, `adjusterContact`, `status` (`#Open` or `#Closed`). Needs write access to the home; at most 50 claims per home (10 when the owner is on the Free plan). This doesn't file a claim or contact the insurer.\n" #
    "- `addInsuranceClaimLog(claimId, date, note)`: adds a dated line to the claim's log (a call, a visit, a letter), up to 200 per claim (50 on the owner's Free plan). Entries can't be edited or removed one by one.\n" #
    "- `deleteInsuranceClaim(claimId)`: deletes a claim record and its log. It can't be undone. Claim records are also removed when the home is transferred.\n" #
    "- `inviteManager(...)` creates an invite link that gives another person access to the property. `removeManager` and `updateManagerRole` change that access.\n" #
    "- `addInventoryItem(propertyId, input)` / `updateInventoryItem(itemId, input)`: add or edit an item in the home's contents inventory: `name` (required, up to 100 characters), `category` (up to 40), `quantity` 1 to 999, `valueCents` (optional, up to $100,000,000), `purchaseDate` (empty, or YYYY-MM-DD from 1900 on), `serialNumber`, `notes`, and `roomId` (a room on this home, or none). Needs write access to the home; at most 500 items per home (100 on the owner's Free plan). This only records what the household enters; HomeGentic doesn't appraise anything or send it to an insurer.\n" #
    "- `deleteInventoryItem(itemId)`: deletes an inventory item. It can't be undone. The inventory is also removed when the home is transferred.\n" #
    "- `setHouseGuide(propertyId, guide)`: saves the home's house guide, or clears it with null, which also ends every link to it. Needs write access to the home. Every field is optional but the guide can't be empty; up to 10 contacts and 6 photo ids. The guide and its links are removed when the home is transferred to a new owner.\n" #
    "- `createHouseGuideLink(propertyId, name, expiryDays)`: creates a link that shows the guide, including any Wi-Fi password and alarm code in it, and the home's street address to anyone who has it, for 1 to 90 days. Needs write access and a saved guide; at most 10 live links per home.\n" #
    "- `revokeHouseGuideLink(token)`: ends a guide link at once. It can't be turned back on; create a new link instead.\n" #
    "- `addArchitecturalReview(propertyId, input)` / `updateArchitecturalReview(reviewId, input)`: log or edit an architectural review request: `project` (required, up to 120 characters), `details`, `submittedDate` and `decisionDate` (YYYY-MM-DD or empty), `status` (`#Planned`, `#Submitted`, `#Approved`, `#ApprovedWithConditions`, `#Denied`, `#Withdrawn`), `conditions`, `approvalDocId`, `jobId`. A submitted request needs its submitted date and a decision needs its decision date. Needs write access; at most 100 per home (25 on the owner's Free plan). Nothing is sent to the association.\n" #
    "- `addSpecialAssessment(propertyId, input)` / `updateSpecialAssessment(assessmentId, input)`: record or edit a special assessment: `title` (required), `amountCents` (more than 0, up to $100,000,000), `dueDate` (YYYY-MM-DD), `paidDate` (YYYY-MM-DD or empty while unpaid), `notes`, `documentId`. Needs write access; at most 100 per home (25 on the owner's Free plan). This doesn't pay anything.\n" #
    "- `deleteArchitecturalReview(reviewId)` / `deleteSpecialAssessment(assessmentId)`: delete a record. It can't be undone. Review requests, assessments and the condo record stay with the home when it is transferred.\n" #
    "- `setCondoAssociationRecord(propertyId, record)`: saves the condo association's milestone inspection and reserve study dates, document ids and notes as the owner knows them, or clears them with null. Condo homes only; needs write access.\n" #
    "- `setHomeWarrantyPlan(propertyId, plan)`: saves the home warranty plan, or clears it with null. Needs write access. `provider` is required (up to 100 characters), `renewalDate` a real date written YYYY-MM-DD, `startDate` the same or empty, the service-call fee up to $1,000. The plan is removed when the home is transferred; its claims stay with the home.\n" #
    "- `addHomeWarrantyClaim(propertyId, input)` / `updateHomeWarrantyClaim(claimId, input)`: log or edit a claim: `issue` (required, up to 120 characters), `dateFiled` (YYYY-MM-DD), `claimNumber`, `jobId`, `serviceFeePaidCents`, `outcome` (`#Open`, `#Approved`, `#PartlyApproved`, `#Denied`, `#Withdrawn`) and notes. Needs write access; at most 100 per home (25 on the owner's Free plan). Nothing is filed with the company.\n" #
    "- `deleteHomeWarrantyClaim(claimId)`: deletes a claim record. It can't be undone.\n" #
    "- `setMortgageLoan(propertyId, loan)`: saves the owner's mortgage numbers, or clears them with null. Owner and co-owners only. Amount borrowed more than 0 and up to $100,000,000, rate up to 30%, term 12 to 480 months, first payment date YYYY-MM-DD; a statement balance needs its date and can't be more than the amount borrowed. The details are removed when the home is transferred.\n" #
    "- `setPropertyTaxYear(propertyId, input)`: saves one tax year's values and exemption status, replacing that year if it's saved. Owner and co-owners only. `year` 1950 to 2100, each value up to $1,000,000,000, `petitionDeadline` empty or a real date in that tax year written YYYY-MM-DD, notes up to 1,000 characters; at most 60 years per home. It only records what the owner enters: it doesn't file an exemption or a petition. The years are removed when the home is transferred.\n" #
    "- `deletePropertyTaxYear(propertyId, year)`: deletes one saved tax year. Owner and co-owners only. It can't be undone.\n" #
    "- `startMoveInPlan(propertyId)`: starts a move-in plan on the home, or returns the one it has. Needs write access. A buyer who claims a home through a transfer gets a fresh plan; the seller's plan isn't passed on.\n" #
    "- `setMoveInStep(propertyId, stepId, done)`: marks a step, or a task by its id, done or not done. Step ids are 1 to 64 letters, digits, '-' or '_'. Needs write access and a plan.\n" #
    "- `addMoveInTasks(propertyId, tasks)`: adds 1 to 25 tasks to the plan (`title` required, up to 120 characters; `detail` up to 500; `area` up to 40; `urgency`). At most 60 tasks on a plan. Needs write access.\n" #
    "- `deleteMoveInTask(propertyId, taskId)` / `endMoveInPlan(propertyId)`: delete one task, or remove the whole plan. Neither can be undone.\n" #
    "- `setSuccessor(propertyId, successor)`: names the person who can claim the home record if the owner dies or the home passes to a trust or heir (`name` required, up to 100 characters; a valid `email`; `relationship` up to 60). Owner only. Each call issues a new successor link and the old one stops working. `removeSuccessor(propertyId)` removes it. Neither is allowed while a claim is open. HomeGentic doesn't email the successor; the owner gives them the link.\n" #
    "- `openSuccessionClaim(token, claim, proof)`: the successor asks for the record, with a proof document (`proofKind`: `#DeathCertificate`, `#LettersOfAdministration`, `#LettersTestamentary` or `#TrustDocument`; a PDF, JPEG or PNG of at most 1.8 MB). One open claim per home; the owner can't open one. The owner and co-owners are emailed at once.\n" #
    "- `cancelSuccessionClaim(claimId)`: ends an open claim. The owner, a co-owner, the claimant or an administrator. The proof document is deleted.\n" #
    "- `reviewSuccessionClaim(claimId, approve, reason)`: administrators only. A rejection needs a reason; its proof document is deleted.\n" #
    "- `completeSuccessionClaim(claimId)`: the claimant takes over the home record, only once the claim is approved and 30 days have passed since it was opened. Like a claimed transfer, the previous household loses access and it can't be reversed; unlike one, the claimant keeps the household's insurance, claims, inventory, house guide, warranty, mortgage and tax records and its personal documents. This passes on the HomeGentic record only: it doesn't transfer the property or act in any estate or probate matter.\n" #
    "- Ownership transfers (`initiateTransfer`, `claimTransfer`, `cancelTransfer`) hand the home and its record to a new owner. The previous household's closing, title, deed, insurance, HOA and other personal documents, and its insurance-claim and inventory photos, stay private to whoever uploaded them; work records and job photos go with the home. A successor who completes a succession claim inherits everything, personal documents included. A transfer can't be reversed once claimed.\n\n" #
    Shared.common()
  };
};
